1) Reverse Words in a String : 
   ==========================

BruteForce Approach: Isme use kiye hai ArrayList ko aur StringBuilder ko StringBuilder se use karke pura word bana rahe hai , Aur pure word ko list mein daal rahe hai aur phir list ko reverse kar rahe hai , isse kya ho raha hai characters reverse nhi honge kyuki list mein ek pura word hai 

code:  class Solution {
    public String reverseWords(String s) {
        List<String> words = new ArrayList<>();
        StringBuilder word = new StringBuilder();
        for(int i=0;i<s.length();i++)
        {
            if(s.charAt(i)!=' ')
            {
                word.append(s.charAt(i));
            }
            else if(word.length()>0)   // naya word le rahe hai khali karke StringBuilder ko 
            {
                words.add(word.toString());
                word.setLength(0);
            }
        }
        if(word.length()>0)
        {
            words.add(word.toString()); // last word bacha reh jayega isliye
        }
        Collections.reverse(words);
        return String.join(" ",words); // join kar rahe hai saare words ko space ke saath
    }
}   

Complexity Analysis

Time Complexity: O(N),We traverse the string once to collect words (O(N)) and once more to reverse and join them (O(N)). Hence total time is O(N).

Space Complexity: O(N),We store all words in a separate list/array, requiring extra space proportional to the number of characters.


Optimal Approach: Ab ek naya space use nhi karenge store karne ke liye, piche se iteration shuru kar rahe hai Jab tak word na mil jaye(space ignore karke ) Aur jaise hi word mila ab , us word pe tak tak traverse karenge jab tak space na mil jaye iska matlab pura word nikal rahe hai , Traversal ke through aur substring function use karke pura word daal denge , ek hi baar mein store, no reversal nothing .
                  Isme sab kaam piche se ho raha hai, kyuki piche se hi word nikal ke kaam karna hai

code: class Solution {
    public String reverseWords(String s) {
        StringBuilder result = new StringBuilder();
        int i = s.length()-1;
        while(i>=0)
        {
            while(i>=0 && s.charAt(i) == ' '){
                i--;
            }

            if(i<0) break;

            int end = i;

            while(i>=0 && s.charAt(i) != ' ')
            {
                i--;
            }

            String word = s.substring(i + 1, end + 1);

            if (result.length() > 0) {
                result.append(" ");
            }
            result.append(word);
        }
        return result.toString();
    }
}                    

Complexity Analysis

Time Complexity: O(N), We traverse the string once from right to left and construct the result directly without extra passes.

Space Complexity: O(1),Ignoring the output string, no additional data structures proportional to input size are used.




